## Task board (Ordna)
- Tasks are markdown files in `tasks/` (`ordna list`, `ordna show <id>`); config in `.ordna/config.yaml`; upstream agent guide in `AGENTS.md`. The `ordna-tasks` skill defines the model and wins over `AGENTS.md`.
- Columns (`statuses` in `.ordna/config.yaml`), **one per agent role, so the board shows which agent has a story**: `todo` → `general-planning` (the solution's general documents; business-analyst, architect and test-manager in turn) → `business-design` (business-analyst) → `technical-design` (architect) → `test-design` (test-manager) → `development` (developer; includes the unit tests) → `functional-test` (tester) → `perf-test` (perf-tester, skipped for a story with no performance criterion) → `done`. A card sits in the column of the agent who has it now, and the assignee is that agent (`todo` = nobody has claimed it yet; `done` = closed by the lead). An agent claims a card (`ordna assign`, `ordna move`) before working on it and hands it to the next agent's column when finished. **The `development` column is entered only by the developer's own claim, after `check-approval.sh` passes for the feature**; the test-manager hands a planned story to `todo` (assignee `developer`).
- One card per user story (`US-N`, walking skeleton `S0`), one requirements card per feature and one general-planning card per solution (tags `planning`, `general`, created by the lead, kept in `general-planning`, assignee changes with the document being written); no epic, `dev`, `verify` or `defect` cards. Tick criteria and checklist items one by one at the moment they hold, never in a batch.
- Every agent claims its card before starting, updates it as the work changes state, and never moves its own work to `done`; the lead closes cards. Nobody runs `ordna commit`; the lead commits.
- Check: `.claude/scripts/check-board.sh` (installed by the kit).

## Documents (one authoritative file each)
- General architecture: docs/architecture.md (**only what is valid for all features**: layout, tooling, cross-cutting rules, general ADRs, the S0 walking skeleton; nothing feature-specific)
- Per feature, in docs/features/e-N-<slug>/: business-prd.md (business-analyst), technical-prd.md (architect: data model, API, design, feature ADRs, slice plan), test-plan.md (test-manager: test cases and test data)
- Test strategy: docs/test-strategy.md (test-manager; general, same level as architecture.md)
- **Every feature has exactly three documents** in docs/features/e-N-<slug>/: `business-prd.md`, `technical-prd.md`, `test-plan.md`. The test plan is specific to its feature.
- **No overlap between `test-strategy.md` and `test-plan.md`.** The strategy holds only what is true for every feature and never names a feature, criterion id (`US-N.m`), endpoint, screen, dataset or case; it defines the levels, tools, environments, how test data is created, isolated and reset in general, naming, coverage gates, the general entry and exit criteria, defect handling and manual coverage. The plan holds only what is specific to its feature: its cases, its named datasets with exact values and volumes, its exploratory charters, its criterion-to-case traceability and its risks, and it links to the strategy instead of restating any of it (a feature-specific deviation from the strategy is stated once, in the plan, as a deviation). Each fact lives in exactly one of the two. The criterion-to-case mapping lives only in the plan.
- TDD evidence: docs/tdd-log.md
- arc42 (optional, summarises architecture.md): docs/arc42/

